/surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Frush</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Minimizing radiation dose for pediatric body applications of single-detector helical CT</article-title><source>AJR Am J Roentgenol</source><year>2001</year><volume>176</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11159061</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cremin</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Radiological assessment of anorectal anomalies</article-title><source>Clin Radiol</source><year>1971</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>250</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5575264</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0009-9260(71)80065-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical outcome and long-term quality of life after surgical correction of Hirschsprung's disease</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>1996</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>1496</fpage><lpage>1502</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8943109</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0022-3468(96)90164-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stephens</surname><given-names>FD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Imperforate rectum. A new surgical technique</article-title><source>Med J Australia</source><year>1953</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>202</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13036524</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pe&#x000f1;a</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>deVries</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Posterior sagittal anorectoplasty: important technical considerations and new applications</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>1982</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>796</fpage><lpage>811</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6761417</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0022-3468(82)80448-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hedlund</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Pefia</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodriguez</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Maza</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Long-term anorectal function in imperforate anus treated by a posterior sagittal anorectoplasty: Manometric investigation</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>1992</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>906</fpage><lpage>909</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1640342</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0022-3468(92)90395-N</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arhan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Faverdin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Devroede</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Dubois</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Coupris</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pellerin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Manometric assessment of continence after surgery for imperforate anus</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>1976</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>166</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1263053</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0022-3468(76)90280-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nagashima</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Iwai</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Yanagihara</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Iwata</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sensation in the anal region and rectum after surgery for anorectal malformations</article-title><source>Eur J Pediatr Surg</source><year>1995</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>169</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7547805</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kubota</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Suita</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessment of Sphincter Muscle Function Before and After Posterior Sagittal Anorectoplasty Using a Magnetic Spinal Stimulation Technique</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>2002</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>617</fpage><lpage>622</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11912522</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/jpsu.2002.31621</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Langemeijer</surname><given-names>RATM</given-names></name><name><surname>Molenaar</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Continence after posterior sagittal anorectoplasty</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>1991</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>587</fpage><lpage>590</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2061815</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0022-3468(91)90713-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Georgeson</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Inge</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Albanese</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Laparoscopically assisted anorectal pull-through for high imperforate anus-A new technique</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>2000</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>927</fpage><lpage>931</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10873037</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/jpsu.2000.6925</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sydorak</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Albanese</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Laparoscopic repair of high imperforate anus</article-title><source>Semin Pediatr Surg</source><year>2002</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>225</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12407503</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/spsu.2002.35358</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Belizon</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Levitt</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Shoshany</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Pena</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rectal prolapse following posterior sagittal anorectoplasty for anorectal malformations</article-title><source>J Pediatr Surg</source><year>2005</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>192</fpage><lpage>196</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15868584</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jpedsurg.2004.09.035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Bajpai</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://paediatric-urologyonline.com"/></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>